---
import SiteLayout from '../layouts/SiteLayout.astro';

---

<SiteLayout
  title="Privacy Policy | Study Hub"
  description="Learn how Study Hub handles information when you browse resources, use study tools, send suggestions, or contribute learning materials."
>
  <main class="legal-page">
    <header class="legal-page-heading">
      <p class="eyebrow">Privacy and data use</p>
      <h1>Privacy Policy</h1>
      <p>This policy describes the information handled by Study Hub’s public learning library, reader, AI study tools, suggestions board, and resource contributions.</p>
      <p class="policy-updated">Last updated <time datetime="2026-10-14">October 14, 2026</time></p>
    </header>

    <article class="legal-copy">
      <section>
        <h2>1. About Study Hub</h2>
        <p>Study Hub is a public educational resource service. You can browse the library without creating an account. Its catalogue includes learning materials across subjects and levels, with dedicated subject pages currently available for Biology, Chemistry, Mathematics, and Physics. This policy describes the site’s current features and may change as the service develops.</p>
      </section>

      <section>
        <h2>2. Information you provide</h2>
        <p>If you create a Study Hub account with email and password, the account service receives your name, email address, and password, and stores your selected class, subjects, and onboarding status in the account profile. Passwords are stored as password hashes, not readable passwords. If you use Google sign-in, Google shares a verified account identifier, name, and email address with Study Hub; your Google password is never sent to Study Hub. The Google sign-in button opens Google’s account selection flow; Study Hub cannot read or enumerate the browser’s saved Google accounts. After a successful sign-in, this browser may remember the account email only to offer a “Continue as” shortcut. That email is not an authentication credential and can be removed with the forget control. The authentication token stays in the current tab’s session storage, is removed when the tab closes, and has a 30-day maximum lifetime as a server-side safety limit. Bookmarks and individual document votes are saved to your account; aggregate thumbs-up/down percentages and successful resource-share counts are visible to everyone. Share counts are not linked to account identities. If you request paid document delivery, Study Hub stores the sender phone number and request status to verify the payment and keep its download available from your account. Historical payment requests may retain transaction and payment-message data collected under an earlier version of checkout. GitHub Pages and Render are on different sites, so Study Hub does not use cross-site authentication cookies. You do not need an account to browse public learning resources.</p>
        <p>The suggestions board asks for suggestion text and does not request your name or email address. Suggestions are reviewed before they may appear publicly. Do not include personal, confidential, or sensitive information in a suggestion.</p>
        <p>If you submit a learning resource, Study Hub receives the file and the details entered with it so the material can be reviewed and managed. Submissions are not published automatically. Files accepted for the public library may be made accessible to other visitors. Submit only material you are entitled to share.</p>
        <p>If you contact Study Hub by email, we receive the email address and the information in your message so we can respond and handle your request.</p>
      </section>

      <section>
        <h2>3. Reader and browser storage</h2>
        <p>The site stores some reader preferences, bookmarks, and browsing progress in your browser so you can continue using the reader or return to a previous position. This information is kept on the browser and device where it was saved; clearing that browser’s site data may remove it.</p>
      </section>

      <section>
        <h2>4. AI study tools</h2>
        <p>When you submit a question to the AI study companion, the visible PDF page image, your question, and recent conversation context are sent to Study Hub’s AI service and then to Google Gemini to generate a response. In AI Study, your selected class and subjects may also be sent with a request to tailor explanations; your account email and password are not sent to Gemini. This information is sent when you use an AI feature, not merely by opening the reader. Do not submit personal, confidential, or sensitive information. AI responses may be incomplete or incorrect and should be checked against trusted learning materials.</p>
      </section>

      <section>
        <h2>5. Service providers and external content</h2>
        <p>Study Hub uses GitHub Pages to host the website and Supabase for its resource catalogue, submitted resources, and suggestions board. The AI study companion uses Study Hub’s backend service and Google Gemini. These providers may process technical information such as an IP address, device and browser details, and request information when your browser connects to their services. Each provider handles information under its own terms and privacy notices.</p>
        <p>The site loads fonts from Google Fonts and includes learning pages with YouTube embeds or links. Google AdSense code is also present on some subject pages. Loading these services may send connection and page information to the relevant provider; Google’s advertising services may use cookies or similar identifiers as described in Google’s notices and settings. Advertising behaviour may vary with page and account settings.</p>
      </section>

      <section>
        <h2>6. Retention and requests</h2>
        <p>Study Hub keeps suggestions, submitted resources, and related details while they are needed to review and operate the library, respond to requests, and address rights or safety concerns. Hosting and service providers may also retain operational logs or backups under their own schedules. Study Hub does not publish a fixed retention period for every provider record.</p>
        <p>For a question or request about information you provided, email <a href="mailto:trusteth777@gmail.com">trusteth777@gmail.com</a>. Identify the relevant page, suggestion, or resource where possible, and avoid including passwords or other sensitive details.</p>
      </section>

      <section>
        <h2>7. Learners and children</h2>
        <p>Study Hub is intended for learners, including school-age students. Do not enter a learner’s personal, confidential, or sensitive information into suggestions, contribution details, or AI prompts. A parent, guardian, or learner may contact Study Hub with a privacy question or request.</p>
      </section>

      <section>
        <h2>8. Changes to this policy</h2>
        <p>Study Hub may update this policy when features, service providers, or advertising arrangements change. The date above identifies the latest revision. Please review this page periodically.</p>
      </section>
    </article>
  </main>
</SiteLayout>
